.idea
.gradle
.java-version
build

.env.*
# ...but the templates are the point: they show what is needed without showing what it is.
!.env.*.example

# ⛔ `.env.*` DOES NOT MATCH BARE `.env`, NOR AN EDITOR/FINDER DUPLICATE.
# Measured 2026-09-04 with `git check-ignore -v` against the filenames actually in use: every
# `.env.<network>` was covered and `.env` itself was NOT. docker-compose's own convention is a
# bare `.env`, and `docker/.env` is only covered by docker/.gitignore — a root one was one
# `git add -A` from the remote. The " copy" form is the one that has already leaked a wallet
# mnemonic on another repo: a duplicate nobody names and no pattern anticipated.
# ⚠ Kept as explicit names rather than a blanket `.env*`, which would leave the tracked
# `.env.preview.example` / `docker/.env.example` tracked-but-ignored — a state that reads as a
# mistake and invites a "fix" that untracks them.
.env
.env copy
.env*copy*
.env.bak

# Session-local agent state; never belongs in the repo.
.claude/
